<title>USA: Florida citrus groves still in very good condition.</title>
<headline>Florida citrus groves still in very good condition.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida citrus groves, trees and new crop fruit remain in very good to excellent condition, the Florida Agricultural Statistics Service (FASS) said.</p>
<p>Most areas of the citrus belt had ample rain through the first week of September, then benefitted from dry conditions through Sunday, September 15.</p>
<p>New foliage remains on most young trees, FASS said.</p>
<p>Meantime, some growers are irrigating on the high sand hills to maintain good surface moisture levels, and fresh fruit packing houses are testing fruit for early picking.</p>
<p>Growers are applying fall herbicides and milticides between rains.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640</p>
</text>
